[Music]  the evil within - was announced at this  year's e3 with a wonderfully weird  trailer and to my surprise I find myself  pretty excited it's surprising because I  actually didn't like the evil within all  that much but I do believe a lot of the  game's imagery and ideas has the  potential to make a truly great horror  game which is why I'm glad developer  tango GameWorks is getting a second  chance with the sequel coming in only a  few months now's the perfect time to  take a look at where the original fell  short and my hopes for the evil within -  but let's quickly get something out of  the way the evil within most obvious  problem and the one that got the most  attention during its launch was those  pesky black bars it was an attempt to  give the game a cinematic look by  replicating movie aspect ratios lots of  people didn't care for this with  fan-made fixes popping up and eventually  the devs patched in the ability to  disable it in fact based on the footage  we've seen from the evil within - they  seem to have abandoned the black bars  altogether so don't really have to worry  about that okay got that out of the way  now when it comes to horror action games  the balance between these two genres has  always been delicate in the case of the  evil within the to feel at odds with  each other the tense atmosphere built up  in the game's opening hospital scene is  deflated by the blockbuster style city  destroying cutscene five minutes later  and the games more hectic combat  sequences feels hampered by the games of  very limited ammo and claustrophobic  camera there are moments where the  horror and action are blended well like  this early sequence in a village but a  lot of times the game swings wildly  between the two I would love to see the  evil within to strike a far more  consistent balance with its horror and  action another in ballast evil within  has comes from these styles of gameplay  it uses there are primarily three types  of situations unkillable enemies that  you must hide or run from areas where  you must either stealth or shoot through  and waves of enemies you have to fight  and none of these feel as good to play  as a game that just does one of these  really  well the AI you were hiding from seems  like they are moving on a pre-arranged  track and feels more like you're  avoiding a scripted animatronic robot  than an intelligent monster the stealth  gets the job done but it's pretty  simplistic hide throw a bottle stab and  repeat and once you get caught you have  no choice but to engage in combat which  means if you're low on bullets better to  just die in reload and the shooting  itself is fine in sections with solo  enemies but starts to feel clunky and  too imprecise when dealing with a large  horde and the limited ammo can make  these moments feel very unforgiving in a  controller throwing kind of way rather  than a creepy tense kind of way like  it's supposed to I want to see evil  within to improve all of this make the  AI more threatening and clever when  hiding improve the stealth by giving  more options to run away and hide and if  you're gonna make me fight mandatory  large hordes give me better controls and  just a little bit more ammo  all these gameplay styles also feel  isolated from one another and are  separated into very identifiable video  game sections you enter a new room where  the game is basically saying hey it's  time to shoot these guys and then you  went to another room where it says and I  got to run away from this guy because he  can't be killed why well that's just  what's happening in this room it's less  about player choice on how to solve the  situation and rather figuring out  exactly what the developer wants you to  do and doing it which is why I'm really  excited about what even within two is  calling these new less linear areas you  get an open space to explore and find  supplies while avoiding or dealing with  enemies we haven't seen this in action  but it sounds like it has the potential  to take these elements of hiding stealth  and combat and letting the player decide  which of these is the best course of  action  [Applause]  and finally there's the story the first  game story is hot garbage the characters  are never giving any meaningful traits  or motivations there is no understanding  of what is happening in the plot and  what your goal is for the vast majority  of the game like really you just walk  from one scary set piece to the next  with little undercurrent of theme  zombies a village hospital scary armed  lady it's all well-made sleepy stuff and  I give them credit for not resorting to  jump scares but nothing really ties it  together in any meaningful way  it's just horror things  [Music]  thankfully evil within two's premise  already seems to be on the path towards  addressing this yes detective Sebastian  Castellanos returns as the main  character but he was such a non  personality that they have a chance to  really start over with him  the premise is about his dead daughter a  minor thread that was touched upon in  the original game turns out she's not  dead and he has to delve back into the  twisted nightmare world to save her  already we have a clear motive for the  character and the player that has good  potential for personal investment in the  story there also appears to be more of a  theme in the horror and scares  themselves the trailer and promotional  imagery of the game focuses on this  white substance and camera lenses how  this relates to Sebastian's daughter  remains to be seen but it's already more  interesting than the original evil with  ins general theme of horror I'm reminded  of Silent Hill 2 and how one of the  reasons its horror is so memorable is  because it's all directly tied into the  trauma of protagonist James and his wife  everything from the enemy designed to  side characters all tied back to that  relationship if evil within to can use  its imagery to the same effect with  Sebastian and his daughter they can  create some genuinely haunting horror I  do have one very specific request though  please keep Claire de Lune it was the  best part of the first game  [Music]  the original evil within is a great idea  of a game with a talented group of  developers behind it but it suffered  from a lack of focus and original  identity opting to try and be all the  horror games at once  the evil within - is a chance to give  the series its own unique mark if they  can improve and expand on the stealth  aspects tone down some of the combat  sequences and have the story really take  advantage of the personal investment  between Sebastian and his daughter I  will be pretty happy I hope they can  pull it off and we won't have long to  wait because the evil within - comes out  on October 13th which means we are sure  to have more coverage soon so subscribe  to GameSpot so you don't miss anything  seriously though like key Kirkland  [Music]  you

